<p>
    <strong>Core Gameplan:</strong> Game 1 represents a high-velocity
    race to determine who establishes the foundational <a
        href="#"
        class="card-hover"
        data-card-name="Opalescence">Opalescence</a
    > plus <a
        href="#"
        class="card-hover"
        data-card-name="Parallax Wave">Parallax Wave</a
    > lock first. Establishing early defensive presence via <a
        href="#"
        class="card-hover"
        data-card-name="Seal of Cleansing">Seal of Cleansing</a
    > is mandatory to hold an opposing combo attempt hostage on the
    stack.
</p>
<p>
    <strong>Sideboard Strategy:</strong> Post-board structural dynamics
    undergo a complete transformation. Many competitive competitors
    instinctively bring in <a
        href="#"
        class="card-hover"
        data-card-name="Exalted Angel">Exalted Angel</a
    > or <a
        href="#"
        class="card-hover"
        data-card-name="Meddling Mage">Meddling Mage</a
    >, but <strong
        >Angels are fundamentally disastrous in the mirror</strong
    >—they present slow targets that are effortlessly
    permanently exiled by an opposing <a
        href="#"
        class="card-hover"
        data-card-name="Parallax Wave">Parallax Wave</a
    > or cleanly answered by <a
        href="#"
        class="card-hover"
        data-card-name="Swords to Plowshares"
        >Swords to Plowshares</a
    >.
</p>
<p>
    The indisputable post-board MVPs are <a
        href="#"
        class="card-hover"
        data-card-name="Abeyance">Abeyance</a
    > and <a
        href="#"
        class="card-hover"
        data-card-name="Seal of Cleansing">Seal of Cleansing</a
    >. Abeyance cleanly insulates your own <a
        href="#"
        class="card-hover"
        data-card-name="Replenish">Replenish</a
    > resolution or completely shuts off their setup turn, while Seal
    grants immediate instant-speed authority over their enchantments.
    Keep all copies of Exalted Angel and Meddling Mage out of your
    post-board configuration.
</p>
